<title>INDIA: India's Bajaj Auto 1996/97 net higher.</title>
<headline>India's Bajaj Auto 1996/97 net higher.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-05-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to March 31, 1997</p>
<p>	     (in million rupees unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit	     4,405.7  vs   4,181.2</p>
<p>    Sales		   32,441.2  vs  27,938.0</p>
<p>    Other income	   2,099.8  vs   1,382.4</p>
<p>    Total income	  34,541.0  vs  29,320.4</p>
<p>    Expenditure	   26,518.5  vs  22,533.1</p>
<p>    Interest		    73.1  vs	99.0</p>
<p>    Gross profit	   7,949.4  vs   6,688.3</p>
<p>    Depreciation	   1,178.7  vs     737.1</p>
<p>    Tax			2,365.0  vs   1,770.0</p>
<p>    Shr (in rupees)	  55.28  vs     52.37</p>
<p>    Div (in rupees)	  10.00  vs     10.00</p>
<p>Note - Bajaj Auto Ltd, which is India's biggest scooter maker, said it has called a board meeting on May 19 to consider a bonus equity issue.</p>
<p>Vehicles sales rose 1,422,849 units in the latest year from 1,307,211 units in 1995/96 while output grew to 1,439,174 units from 1,302,031 units, the firm said.</p>
<p>Exports fell to 1.58 billion rupees from 1.89 billion.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265-9000</p>
</text>
